__**OP-AMP as an integrator**__

A capacitor present in the feedback path of the OP-AMP makes it work like an integrator.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/67157aa47a379549439a9f163a781cbef0c09d54cf8eac374dc47368a68a84d8.png] 

The transfer of the inverting OP-AMP is given by:

{{V_o}(s)over Vᵢₙ(s)}=-{Z₂over Z₁}

{{V_o}(s)over Vᵢₙ(s)}=-{1/sCover Rᵢₙ}

{{V_o}(s)over Vᵢₙ(s)}=-{1over sRᵢₙC}

∵ {1over s}=int dt

{{V_o}(t)}=-{1over RᵢₙC}int{Vᵢₙ(t)}space dt

